# Velocity Project Conventions

Next.js 15 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4. Always follow the patterns below so new work matches existing code.

## Folder Architecture

- `src/app/` — routing only. Pages stay thin and render a module: `const Page = () => <Home />;`. Keep all UI/logic out of here.
- `src/modules/<feature>/` — feature code. Entry is `index.tsx`; section/sub-components live in `components/<sectionName>/`.
- `src/components/` — shared, cross-feature code: `ui/` (primitives like `button`) and `layouts/` (`header`, `footer`).
- `src/styles/` — `globals.css`, `theme.css` (Tailwind v4 `@theme` tokens), `font.ts`.
- Route page → module `index.tsx` → section `components/<name>/index.tsx` → split sub-components. Don't bypass this layering.

## Naming Conventions

- **Folders + non-component files: `camelCase`** (`aboutSection/`, `joinUs/`, `imageBox.tsx`, `marqueeRow.tsx`, `ctaSection.tsx`). This is the required convention — do not introduce `kebab-case` or `snake_case` files.
- Section/feature entry file is always `index.tsx`.
- Exported React components are `PascalCase` even though the file is `camelCase` (file `featureCard.tsx` → `export default FeatureCard`).
- Variables, functions, props, handlers: `camelCase`; event handlers prefixed `handle` (`handlePrevClick`).
- Types/interfaces: `PascalCase`, props interfaces suffixed `Props` (`FeatureCardProps`).

## Imports

- Use the `@/` alias for everything under `src/` (`@/components/ui/button`, `@/styles/font`). Use relative paths only for sibling files and `public/` assets.
- Use `next/image` for images and `next/link` for internal navigation — never raw `<img>`/`<a>` for internal routes.

## Tooling (must pass)

- Prettier: single quotes, semicolons, 2-space indent, `printWidth` 100, `trailingComma: es5`.
- ESLint extends `next/core-web-vitals` + `next/typescript`; `no-console` and `no-unused-vars` are warnings — keep output clean.
- `lint-staged` + Husky run `eslint --fix` and `prettier --write` on commit. Run `npm run lint` / `npm run format` before finishing.
- TypeScript is `strict`. No `any`; type all props and state.

## After Any Change

- Keep the `README.md` updated when structure, scripts, conventions, or features change.
